WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.780 --> 00:00:05.040
Superhero movies have dominated the box office,
but it's rare for them to be honored with

00:00:05.040 --> 00:00:09.560
nominations in the major Academy Awards categories
- let alone the biggest one of all.

00:00:09.910 --> 00:00:13.980
With that in mind, here's a look at how Black
Panther made history, and how this marks a

00:00:13.980 --> 00:00:15.540
turning point for the Oscars.

00:00:15.980 --> 00:00:17.120
"This never gets old.”

00:00:24.440 --> 00:00:28.780
We've all become accustomed to Marvel's refusal
to settle for superficial storylines in their

00:00:28.780 --> 00:00:29.280
films.

00:00:29.280 --> 00:00:33.020
There's no shortage of modern action movies
that end up feeling like little more than

00:00:33.040 --> 00:00:36.940
an excuse to unload a pile of cash on CGI
and special effects.

00:00:37.110 --> 00:00:41.700
The MCU, on the other hand, has figured out
how to combine large-scale effects with meaningful

00:00:41.710 --> 00:00:44.690
plots, deep drama, and complex characters.

00:00:44.690 --> 00:00:47.080
Nowhere is this more apparent than in Black
Panther.

00:00:47.280 --> 00:00:52.280
Black Panther's onscreen arc started in Captain
America: Civil War, which led to the solo

00:00:52.280 --> 00:00:56.720
film beginning with T'Challa already having
taken up the mantle of the hero of Wakanda.

00:00:56.909 --> 00:01:01.760
Black Panther was still essentially an origin
story, marking the true beginning of the King

00:01:01.760 --> 00:01:02.560
of Wakanda's story.

00:01:02.740 --> 00:01:07.500
As the story unfolded it didn't skimp on the
drama, either, continuing to evolve T'Challa's

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:12.250
persona as he struggled with his past, revelations
regarding his father, and the repercussions

00:01:12.250 --> 00:01:14.100
of long-held family secrets.

00:01:14.240 --> 00:01:19.040
From personal storylines to the introduction
of Wakanda, the film's story was masterfully

00:01:19.049 --> 00:01:23.390
told, and the film's nominations will only
pave the way for future superhero films of

00:01:23.390 --> 00:01:25.680
the same caliber to earn the Academy's attention.

00:01:26.500 --> 00:01:30.480
Even the best scripts can often feel pointless
if they aren't brought to life by quality

00:01:30.480 --> 00:01:34.240
acting, and Black Panther knocked this one
out of the park in spades.

00:01:34.440 --> 00:01:38.800
Front and center, of course, we have the lovable
yet tough Chadwick Boseman, who was able to

00:01:38.880 --> 00:01:42.060
depict T'Challa as a character with a fierceness
of resolve.

00:01:42.360 --> 00:01:46.380
But along with that he also brought a depth
of feeling, understanding, and complexity

00:01:46.380 --> 00:01:48.120
that helped elevate the entire movie.

00:01:48.500 --> 00:01:53.010
Of course, Boseman's supporting cast was also
filled with talented actors - modern cinema

00:01:53.010 --> 00:01:56.800
staples like Andy Serkis, who played returning
villain Ulysses Klaue.

00:01:57.600 --> 00:02:01.160
"You can go, but just don't tell anyone, alright?"

00:02:05.400 --> 00:02:09.619
The film also featured up and coming stars
like Letitia Wright, who delivered a memorable

00:02:09.620 --> 00:02:11.780
performance as T'Challa's sister Shuri.

00:02:12.000 --> 00:02:16.700
And then there's Michael B. Jordan, whose
Killmonger isn't just impressive, he's heart-wrenching.

00:02:17.060 --> 00:02:21.720
In just over two hours Jordan managed to create
a personality that rivals the multi-movie

00:02:21.720 --> 00:02:25.080
character arc of Loki and the dramatic complexity
of Thanos.

00:02:25.480 --> 00:02:29.680
Few would argue that the movie's long list
of quality performances was another crucial

00:02:29.680 --> 00:02:32.340
factor that launched the film into the Academy's
ballots.

00:02:33.260 --> 00:02:38.060
While acting, directing, and storytelling
are all aspects of the film weren't specifically

00:02:38.069 --> 00:02:42.819
honored by the Academy Awards, a quick glance
at the various nominations continues to reveal

00:02:42.820 --> 00:02:45.090
just how thoroughly the movie left its impact.

00:02:45.140 --> 00:02:49.580
Two of the nominations came for Sound Editing
and Sound Mixing, and it racked up two more

00:02:49.590 --> 00:02:51.790
for Original Score and Original Song.

00:02:51.790 --> 00:02:53.540
The quartet speaks for itself.

00:02:53.540 --> 00:02:57.960
The audible experience of Black Panther, from
the sound effects to the music, was superbly

00:02:57.960 --> 00:02:58.460
executed.

00:02:58.960 --> 00:03:00.240
"Wakanda forever!”

00:03:00.500 --> 00:03:02.060
“Wakanda forever!”

00:03:05.260 --> 00:03:10.000
Two more nominations were landed in the categories
of Production Design and Costume Design, both

00:03:10.010 --> 00:03:13.460
of which speak to the film's impressive array
of scenery and clothing.

00:03:13.460 --> 00:03:17.230
All of these recognitions are neatly wrapped
up with the Best Picture nomination which

00:03:17.230 --> 00:03:20.640
puts a bow on one of the most accomplished
chapters in the MCU.

00:03:20.900 --> 00:03:25.240
While arguments can be made for previous Marvel
films that might have been the first to receive

00:03:25.250 --> 00:03:29.549
the honor of a Best Picture nomination, there's
no question that Black Panther deserved the

00:03:29.549 --> 00:03:31.240
nod on its own merits.

00:03:31.740 --> 00:03:37.760
It's hard to believe that heading into the
2019 Oscar ceremony, the DCEU had won more

00:03:37.760 --> 00:03:42.909
Oscars than the MCU by a whopping score of
one to zero, with the lone win coming in the

00:03:42.909 --> 00:03:47.400
form of Makeup and Hairstyling for everyone's
favorite Oscar-winner, Suicide Squad.

00:03:48.700 --> 00:03:49.200
"...And?"

00:03:49.680 --> 00:03:54.120
But, while the two comic universes have certainly
received the short end of the stick, there

00:03:54.120 --> 00:03:58.420
have been a handful of awards over the decades
given to several superhero classics.

00:03:58.540 --> 00:04:02.840
Perhaps the nearest and dearest to the heart
of Marvel fans was Spider-Man 2, which won

00:04:02.840 --> 00:04:04.560
an award for its visual effects.

00:04:04.680 --> 00:04:09.200
Several years before Suicide Squad, comics
fans were also thrilled to see The Dark Knight

00:04:09.209 --> 00:04:14.630
win two Academy Awards - one for editing and
one for best supporting actor, an honor posthumously

00:04:14.630 --> 00:04:17.180
given to Heath Ledger for his performance
as the Joker.

00:04:22.640 --> 00:04:27.080
However, while the two awards were in many
ways a seminal moment for the superhero genre

00:04:27.080 --> 00:04:31.290
in the Academy's history, perhaps the greater
impact came from the fact that the film wasn't

00:04:31.290 --> 00:04:32.560
nominated for best picture.

00:04:32.950 --> 00:04:37.580
The perceived injustice became a rallying
point for comic fans, in many ways helping

00:04:37.580 --> 00:04:40.600
to pave the way for the achievement that Black
Panther finally realized.

00:04:41.620 --> 00:04:46.340
It's this issue over Best Picture nominations
that has stuck in the craw of so many comics

00:04:46.340 --> 00:04:47.340
fans over the years.

00:04:47.620 --> 00:04:51.980
While there is at least a semi-reasonable
track record of nominations — and wins — for

00:04:51.990 --> 00:04:56.410
technical categories like makeup, sound editing,
and special effects, there has always been

00:04:56.410 --> 00:05:00.820
a serious lack of attention for comic book
adaptations in the Best Picture category.

00:05:01.150 --> 00:05:05.140
While films like The Dark Knight began to
shift the conversation from an "if" to more

00:05:05.150 --> 00:05:09.830
of a "when," the success of other genres should
be taken into account when tracing the path

00:05:09.830 --> 00:05:12.220
leading to Black Panther's historic success.

00:05:12.460 --> 00:05:16.680
For example, it was considered outlandish
when the classic animated film Beauty and

00:05:16.690 --> 00:05:20.050
the Beast was nominated for Best Picture in
the early '90s.

00:05:20.050 --> 00:05:24.690
And yet, since then we've seen films like
Up and Toy Story 3 follow in its footsteps,

00:05:24.690 --> 00:05:28.060
proving that the premise isn't as important
as the heart that holds it up.

00:05:28.260 --> 00:05:32.660
Then there's the fantasy epic Lord of the
Rings: Return of the King, which dominated

00:05:32.660 --> 00:05:37.660
the 76th Academy Awards with a clean sweep,
winning all 11 of the Oscars it was nominated

00:05:37.660 --> 00:05:38.160
for.

00:05:38.320 --> 00:05:42.460
While comics trailblazers have done their
part over time, the "little victories" along

00:05:42.470 --> 00:05:47.419
the way, like the success of Peter Jackson's
monumental trilogy of Tolkien adaptations,

00:05:47.419 --> 00:05:51.701
have certainly helped reshape the landscape,
setting the stage for the Best Picture nomination

00:05:51.701 --> 00:05:55.080
that finally took superhero movies to the
next level of acclaim.

00:05:55.120 --> 00:06:00.140
After all, let's not forget that 2018's Best
Picture winner was a movie about a fish god.

00:06:00.460 --> 00:06:02.920
Why not one about a guy who dresses like a
cat?

00:06:03.500 --> 00:06:08.220
Another factor behind the gradual acceptance
of comic book and superhero-based movies comes

00:06:08.220 --> 00:06:12.220
from a certain level of cinematic maturation
that has taken place over the years.

00:06:12.300 --> 00:06:16.620
It's safe to say that past superhero films
have been, well, kind of cheesy.

00:06:21.340 --> 00:06:25.819
The MCU has been a major factor in pushing
the genre to a more mature level.

00:06:25.819 --> 00:06:30.830
After a long incubation period that saw characters
like Tony Stark, Thor, and Captain America

00:06:30.830 --> 00:06:35.440
finding their stride, the modern concept of
a superhero movie has certainly come a long

00:06:35.440 --> 00:06:35.940
way.

00:06:35.980 --> 00:06:40.960
As the MCU has evolved, it's played on a bigger
canvas and grasped at loftier ambitions as

00:06:40.960 --> 00:06:42.920
well as more complex character arcs.

00:06:43.140 --> 00:06:46.300
This has naturally pushed the end product
to higher levels.

00:06:46.520 --> 00:06:50.740
While that initial growth culminated with
Black Panther's recognition by the Academy,

00:06:50.750 --> 00:06:55.120
it's only a matter of time before we see even
more mature, more accomplished superhero films

00:06:55.120 --> 00:06:57.220
- and see more of them reach the Oscars podium.

00:06:58.480 --> 00:07:01.919
There are many reasons Black Panther broke
through the barrier of acceptance with the

00:07:01.920 --> 00:07:04.020
world's most prestigious awards ceremony.

00:07:04.370 --> 00:07:08.580
The combination of timing and quality has
launched director Ryan Coogler's creation

00:07:08.599 --> 00:07:13.610
into the spotlight as it vies for recognition
that has been denied to so many worthy superhero

00:07:13.610 --> 00:07:14.500
films before.

00:07:14.790 --> 00:07:19.280
The most exciting part about 2019's Academy
Awards, however, is what it might lead to

00:07:19.280 --> 00:07:20.000
next.

00:07:20.300 --> 00:07:24.819
The final acceptance of superhero movies as
awards-worthy entertainment has further opened

00:07:24.819 --> 00:07:28.940
the doors for serious filmmakers and artists
to genuinely invest themselves into their

00:07:28.940 --> 00:07:33.280
comics-to-screen adaptations - not only in
the hopes of garnering the adulation of the

00:07:33.280 --> 00:07:37.160
fans, but of possibly winning a nice shiny
Oscar while they're at it.

00:07:37.340 --> 00:07:39.820
There's only one thing to say to that kind
of future:

00:07:40.060 --> 00:07:42.520
"Let the challenge begin."

